From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: nss_core: trace data buffers coming up from the firmware

The host->firmware direction has been traced for weeks; nothing ever
logged what the firmware hands back. Log every non-status buffer with
the interface number it carries, so it is possible to tell whether the
firmware delivers received frames at all.

DEBUG ONLY - do not submit.

--- a/nss_core.c
+++ b/nss_core.c
@@ -1065,6 +1065,21 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
+	/* DEBUG: every data buffer the firmware hands up, with the interface
+	 * it claims it belongs to. The status stream is excluded - it is the
+	 * periodic sync and would drown the log. First 40 unconditionally,
+	 * then one in a thousand, so a steady stream stays visible.
+	 */
+	if (buffer_type != N2H_BUFFER_STATUS) {
+		static unsigned long nss_dbg_rx_count;
+
+		if (nss_dbg_rx_count < 40 || (nss_dbg_rx_count % 1000) == 0)
+			pr_info("nss-n2h-data: n=%lu if=%u type=%u len=%u\n",
+				nss_dbg_rx_count, interface_num, buffer_type,
+				nbuf->len);
+		nss_dbg_rx_count++;
+	}
+
 	switch (buffer_type) {
 	case N2H_BUFFER_PACKET:
 		nss_core_handle_buffer_pkt(nss_ctx, interface_num, nbuf, napi, desc->bit_flags, qid, desc->service_code);
